==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|longævity||archaic}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂ey-|id=life}}
Early 17th century, {{lbor|en|la|longaevitās|nocap=1}}, from {{af|la|longaevus|-itas|alt2=-itās|gloss1=ancient, aged|nocat=1}}. The first part is related with {{m+|en|long}} and this association led to the alternative pronunciation with {{IPAchar|/ŋ/}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/lɒnˈd͡ʒɛv.ɪ.ti/|/lɒŋ-/|a=UK}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-longevity.wav|a=Southern England|IPA=/lɒnˈd͡ʒɛv.ɪ.ti/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-longevity2.wav|a=Southern England|IPA=/lɒŋˈd͡ʒɛv.ɪ.ti/}}
* {{IPA|en|/lɑnˈd͡ʒɛv.ə.ti/|/lɔn-/|/lɔŋ-/|[ɫɑ̃nˈd͡ʒɛv.ə.ɾi]|[ɫɔ̃n-]|[ɫɔ̃ŋ-]|a=US,CA}}
* {{IPA|en|/lɔŋˈd͡ʒev.ə.ti/|[lɔŋˈd͡ʒev.ə.ɾi]|a=AU}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The quality of being [[long-lasting]], especially of [[life]].
#: {{ux|en|Grandpa had incredible '''longevity''': he lived to be 105 years old!}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2020 July 1|author=David Allen|title=Signalling from Leeds along the S&C|journal=Rail|page=74|text=This 142-year-old tiny ex-LNWR SB <small>[signal box, at Batley]</small> is an amazing survivor, probably owing its '''longevity''' to its location alongside a level crossing. Indeed it started life as a gate box with the delightful name of Lady Ann's Crossing.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Parija Kavilanz|title=‘Swicy’ is the hottest trend in food right now|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2024/06/02/business/spicy-snack-foods-drinks-trend-swicy/index.html|date=2024-06-02|passage=The '''longevity''' of spicy and swicy will depend on how committed consumers are to sticking with these flavors as they grow older.}}
# {{1|duration}} over time; [[persistence]].
#* {{quote-journal|1=en|year=2018|author=James Lambert|title=Anglo-Indian slang in dictionaries on historical principles|journal=World Englishes|volume=37|page=255|text=A ‘postdating’ is an example of the use of a lexical item at a later date than currently recorded and these are important in establishing the '''longevity''' of use of a term and whether or not it has become obsolete.}}

